globalThis.OSLabConcurrencyDownloads = Object.freeze({"concurrency_lab.py":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"OSLab deterministic concurrency exercises; no real threads are created.\n\nRun with Python 3.8+; no third-party packages required. Each printed operation\nis one abstract step. Output is independent of the host OS scheduler and GIL.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\n\n\ndef updates(order):\n    count = 0\n    registers = {\"A\": None, \"B\": None}\n    pcs = {\"A\": 0, \"B\": 0}\n    if len(order) != 6 or order.count(\"A\") != 3 or order.count(\"B\") != 3:\n        raise ValueError(\"order must contain exactly three A and three B\")\n    print(\"initial count=0; expected=2\")\n    for who in order:\n        pc = pcs[who]\n        if pc == 0:\n            registers[who] = count\n            action = \"read\"\n        elif pc == 1:\n            registers[who] += 1\n            action = \"add\"\n        else:\n            count = registers[who]\n            action = \"write\"\n        pcs[who] += 1\n        print(f\"{who} {action:<5} local={registers[who]} shared={count}\")\n    print(f\"final count={count}; expected=2\")\n\n\ndef locks(policy, schedule):\n    owners = {\"L1\": None, \"L2\": None}\n    pcs = {\"A\": 0, \"B\": 0}\n    waiting = {\"A\": None, \"B\": None}\n    completed = 0\n    for turn in range(50):\n        if pcs[\"A\"] == pcs[\"B\"] == 5:\n            break\n        who = (\"A\" if pcs[\"A\"] < 5 else \"B\") if schedule == \"serial\" else \"AB\"[turn % 2]\n        if pcs[who] == 5 or (waiting[who] and owners[waiting[who]]):\n            continue\n        first, second = (\"L2\", \"L1\") if who == \"B\" and policy == \"opposite\" else (\"L1\", \"L2\")\n        op, key = [(\"lock\", first), (\"lock\", second), (\"work\", None), (\"unlock\", second), (\"unlock\", first)][pcs[who]]\n        if op == \"lock\" and owners[key]:\n            waiting[who] = key\n            print(f\"{who} waits for {key} held by {owners[key]}\")\n        else:\n            if op == \"lock\":\n                owners[key] = who\n                waiting[who] = None\n            elif op == \"unlock\":\n                owners[key] = None\n            else:\n                completed += 1\n            pcs[who] += 1\n            print(f\"{who} {op}\" + (f\" {key}\" if key else \"\"))\n        if all(waiting[t] and owners[waiting[t]] for t in (\"A\", \"B\")):\n            print(f\"deadlock=yes; completed={completed}/2\")\n            return\n    print(f\"deadlock=no; completed={completed}/2\")\n\n\ndef events(mode, delay):\n    print(f\"A arrives=0; B arrives=1; I/O delay={delay}\")\n    end = delay + (3 if mode == \"blocking\" else 2)\n    done = {}\n    for t in range(end):\n        if t == 0:\n            action = \"A submits I/O\"\n        elif (mode == \"async\" and t == 1) or (mode == \"blocking\" and t == delay + 2):\n            action = \"B completes\"\n            done[\"B\"] = t + 1\n        elif t == delay + 1:\n            action = \"A resumes and completes\"\n            done[\"A\"] = t + 1\n        else:\n            action = \"loop blocked\" if mode == \"blocking\" else \"loop idle; I/O pending\"\n        print(f\"[{t},{t+1}) {action}\")\n    print(f\"completed A={done['A']}; B={done['B']}\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"exercise\", required=True)\n    update = sub.add_parser(\"updates\", help=\"two three-step counter updates\")\n    update.add_argument(\"--order\", default=\"ABABAB\", help=\"exactly three A and three B\")\n    lock = sub.add_parser(\"locks\", help=\"two threads acquiring two locks\")\n    lock.add_argument(\"--policy\", choices=[\"opposite\", \"ordered\"], default=\"opposite\")\n    lock.add_argument(\"--schedule\", choices=[\"interleaved\", \"serial\"], default=\"interleaved\")\n    event = sub.add_parser(\"events\", help=\"one event loop and two requests\")\n    event.add_argument(\"--mode\", choices=[\"blocking\", \"async\"], default=\"blocking\")\n    event.add_argument(\"--delay\", type=int, choices=[4, 8], default=4)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    if args.exercise == \"updates\":\n        try:\n            updates(args.order)\n        except ValueError as error:\n            parser.error(str(error))\n    elif args.exercise == \"locks\":\n        locks(args.policy, args.schedule)\n    else:\n        events(args.mode, args.delay)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","README.md":"# 并发参考实践程序\n\n`concurrency_lab.py` 是本站的确定性教学模拟器，使用 Python 3.8 及以上版本，不依赖第三方包。可在 Linux 终端运行，也可在具备 Python 3 的其他系统使用。\n\n它不创建真实线程，不展示宿主机实际调度，不测量真实性能。固定次序便于重复分析；错误模型不对应带有未定义行为的 C 程序。\n\n## 运行\n\n下载脚本，在脚本所在目录打开终端：\n\n```sh\npython3 concurrency_lab.py --help\npython3 concurrency_lab.py updates --order ABABAB\npython3 concurrency_lab.py updates --order AAABBB\npython3 concurrency_lab.py locks --policy opposite\npython3 concurrency_lab.py locks --policy ordered\npython3 concurrency_lab.py events --mode blocking --delay 4\npython3 concurrency_lab.py events --mode async --delay 4\n```\n\n## 参数与输出\n\n- `updates --order`：次序字符串恰含三个 A、三个 B。每个线程依次读取、加一、写回。`local` 是线程的局部值，`shared` 是共享值。`ABABAB` 最后为 1，`AAABBB` 最后为 2。\n- `locks --policy opposite|ordered`：分别表示 A 按 L1→L2、B 按 L2→L1，以及双方统一按 L1→L2。默认交替推进；`--schedule serial` 改为 A 完成后 B 执行。`waits for` 表示获取失败后等待；`completed` 只计同时持有两锁后完成的操作。相反次序配合交替推进会形成死锁；相反次序配合依次运行可以结束，不能据此证明方案无死锁风险。\n- `events --mode blocking|async --delay 4|8`：A 在 t=0 到达，B 在 t=1 到达。A 提交和恢复处理各需 1 单位，I/O 另需 delay 单位，B 需 1 单位。每行 `[t,t+1)` 表示一个区间；`completed` 是完成时刻，不是延迟或 CPU 用时。delay=4 时，阻塞方案 A=6、B=7，异步方案 A=6、B=2。`idle` 表示没有就绪事件，可以休眠等待，不要求忙等。\n\n参数不合法会打印用法并以非零状态退出。死锁场景会在识别相互等待后正常打印结论并退出，不会让终端一直挂起。\n\n## 分析方向\n\n先核对逐步输出与对应知识页的共享状态，再改变一个条件进行比较。计数器关注检查或读取的结果何时过期；锁关注等待者同时持有什么；事件循环关注等待 I/O 时能否处理已就绪的其他请求。参考页面还链接条件变量和信号量的队列比较，无需编写完整的线程库或服务器。\n\n## 真实线程对照：锁的保护范围\n\n`thread_counter.c` 在 Linux 中通过 pthread 创建两个真实线程，共同更新一个初值为 0 的计数器。使用已有的 C 编译器编译：\n\n```sh\ncc -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -pthread thread_counter.c -o thread_counter\n./thread_counter whole\n./thread_counter split\n```\n\n- `whole`：锁保护完整的“读取、加一、写回”，末行为 `joined=2; count=2; expected=2`。\n- `split`：读取和写回分别加锁；程序安排两个线程都读完旧值后才继续写回，末行为 `joined=2; count=1; expected=2`。\n\n两个方案每次访问共享计数器时都正确加锁；差别是保护范围。split 中使用一次同步等待来稳定复现“双方都读到 0”的次序，不代表自然调度总会这样安排，也不依赖无锁 C 数据竞争或随机碰运气。完整加锁方案不在持锁期间等待对方读取。\n\n每个线程的输出记录包含 `pid`（进程号）、`tid`（Linux 线程号）、`read`（读到的旧值）和 `wrote`（写回的值）。同一次运行的两个 pid 相同、tid 不同；具体号码随运行变化。主线程在两个 join 都成功返回后统一按 A、B 顺序打印记录，这个显示顺序不代表实际执行先后。\n\n比较两条命令时，关注 join 保证线程已结束，却不能补救此前错误的更新；正确性还取决于锁是否覆盖完整操作。源码可供查看，不要求掌握屏障接口的实现。`./thread_counter --help` 显示参数说明；非法参数以非零状态退出。\n","thread_counter.c":"#define _GNU_SOURCE\n#include <pthread.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <sys/syscall.h>\n#include <unistd.h>\n\n/* Linux/POSIX: real threads, with a controlled interleaving in split mode.\n * All overlapping accesses to count use the same mutex; there is no C data race.\n */\nstatic pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;\nstatic pthread_barrier_t rendezvous;\nstatic int count = 0;\nstatic int split = 0;\n\nstruct observation { char name; long pid, tid; int read, wrote; };\n\nstatic void check(int error, const char *operation) {\n    if (error) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"%s: %s\\n\", operation, strerror(error));\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void meet(void) {\n    int error = pthread_barrier_wait(&rendezvous);\n    if (error != PTHREAD_BARRIER_SERIAL_THREAD) check(error, \"pthread_barrier_wait\");\n}\n\nstatic void *increment(void *argument) {\n    struct observation *o = argument;\n    o->pid = (long)getpid();\n    o->tid = syscall(SYS_gettid);\n    meet(); /* Both real threads exist before either starts the update. */\n\n    check(pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex), \"pthread_mutex_lock\");\n    o->read = count;\n    if (split) {\n        check(pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex), \"pthread_mutex_unlock\");\n        meet(); /* Both threads have read the old value before either writes. */\n        check(pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex), \"pthread_mutex_lock\");\n    }\n    o->wrote = o->read + 1;\n    count = o->wrote;\n    check(pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex), \"pthread_mutex_unlock\");\n    return NULL;\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    if (argc == 2 && strcmp(argv[1], \"--help\") == 0) {\n        puts(\"Usage: ./thread_counter whole|split\\nwhole: lock the complete update\\nsplit: lock read and write separately; synchronize after both reads\");\n        return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n    }\n    if (argc != 2 || (strcmp(argv[1], \"whole\") && strcmp(argv[1], \"split\"))) {\n        fputs(\"Usage: ./thread_counter whole|split\\n\", stderr);\n        return 2;\n    }\n    split = strcmp(argv[1], \"split\") == 0;\n    pthread_t workers[2];\n    struct observation records[2] = {{.name = 'A'}, {.name = 'B'}};\n    check(pthread_barrier_init(&rendezvous, NULL, 2), \"pthread_barrier_init\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i)\n        check(pthread_create(&workers[i], NULL, increment, &records[i]), \"pthread_create\");\n    for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i)\n        check(pthread_join(workers[i], NULL), \"pthread_join\");\n\n    printf(\"mode=%s\\n\", argv[1]);\n    /* Fixed display order, not a claim about the order in which threads ran. */\n    for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {\n        struct observation *o = &records[i];\n        printf(\"%c pid=%ld tid=%ld read=%d wrote=%d\\n\", o->name, o->pid, o->tid, o->read, o->wrote);\n    }\n    printf(\"joined=2; count=%d; expected=2\\n\", count);\n    check(pthread_barrier_destroy(&rendezvous), \"pthread_barrier_destroy\");\n    check(pthread_mutex_destroy(&mutex), \"pthread_mutex_destroy\");\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n"});
